00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:11.380
Turner Tenny, better known
by his Fortnite name of Tfue,

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.210
started a firestorm by
accusing his management group,

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.740
FaZe Clan of an oppressive labor contract.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.130
What is he complaining about

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.820
and is the contract really that bad

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.380
or is Tfue just a greedy
gamer who was bitter

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.200
about signing an unfavorable contract.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.190
The answer could end up
setting legal precedent

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.880
that will determine
the rights of thousands

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.566
of professional gamers
all over the country.

00:00:32.566 --> 00:00:35.066
(light music)

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.530
Hey Legal Eagles, it's time
to think like a lawyer.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:43.839
Today we are adjudicating the
case of Tfue versus FaZe Clan.

00:00:43.839 --> 00:00:45.610
You may know the background here,

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.100
hundreds of millions of people
love playing video games.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.430
Their passion for gaming
has led to the creation

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.760
of a new industry known as
eSports which allows players

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.140
to play competitively for cash prizes.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.620
eSports is a multi-billion
dollar industry.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.660
Professional gamers in 2019
can make millions of dollars,

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.010
live in fancy mansions,
fly on private jets

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.090
and make plenty of money.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.310
Investors are looking to cash in as well

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.230
and are pumping hundreds
of millions of dollars

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.890
into the eSports industry

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.010
which promises to establish
video game leagues

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.030
that will eventually
rival professional sports

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.220
in revenue and public attention

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.490
and when there's billions
of dollars at stake,

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:24.680
that can only mean one thing, lawyers

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.610
which of course leads us to the matter

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:30.660
of Tfue versus FaZe
Clan or is it FaZe Clan.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.300
Capitalization is apparently
hard with these people,

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.610
and anyway, if you're watching this video,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.650
you probably already know who Tfue is.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.850
He is a 21 year old gamer
who is currently one

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.811
of the top Fortnite players in the world.

00:01:40.811 --> 00:01:42.700
Tfue regularly wins Fortnite tournaments,

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.600
has made over half a million
dollars in prize money

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.970
in just 29 tournaments.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.090
He has his own YouTube
channel and is far and away

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:52.020
the most watched Fortnite
streamer on Twitch.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.020
All of this makes him a star on the rise

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.600
in the eSports world.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:56.650
If you're watching this video,

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.020
you probably also know who FaZe Clan is.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.540
It may sound like a mid
90s hip-hop collective,

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.060
but FaZe Clan is actually one

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.060
of the biggest brands in esports.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.580
FaZe Clan bills itself

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.800
as a professional eSports organization.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.500
It has its own or teams with players

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.490
who compete in tournaments for Fortnite,

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.890
Call of Duty and Rainbow Six.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.340
FaZe Clan also sponsors events,

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.580
it has its own Twitch and YouTube streams.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.390
Topping it all off, FaZe Clan reports

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.450
to be a lifestyle brand
which sells T-shirts

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.340
and hats and other items as well.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:28.720
In 2018, FaZe Clan sought
to partner with Tfue,

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.070
culminating in a contract,
a quote gamer agreement

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.690
for Tfue to play for their league.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.680
When Tfue signed the gamer
agreement with FaZe back

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.220
in 2018, he wasn't quite
the star that he is now,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.130
but by 2019, Tfue was dominant at Fortnite

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.330
and has a growing personal brand

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.980
which gave him more opportunities

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.300
and endorsements outside
of the FaZe Clan umbrella.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.600
This is probably where
the party's interests

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.910
may have started to diverge.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.060
Tfue was unhappy and said
that the gamer agreement

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.920
that he signed forced him
to remain with the team

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.150
for three years, stuck in with a salary

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.080
of just 2,000 dollars per month

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.900
and let them keep 50% of most of the fees

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.260
and 20% of his prize money.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.610
He also said that the
contract allowed FaZe Clan

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.100
to take up to 80% of any brand deals

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.780
that were made for
Tfue's personal channels.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.180
That means that if Tfue
signed a deal to run an ad

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.940
on his personal YouTube channel,

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.680
FaZe Clan would get to
keep most of the money.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.100
The founder of FaZe Clan,

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.420
Ricky Banks accused
Tfue of being disloyal.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.240
He said that the company
hadn't taken the 20% cut

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:34.760
of prize money it was entitled
to under the contract.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.170
Banks said that despite
the contract terms,

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.210
FaZe Clan hasn't collected any revenue

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.410
from Tfue's tournament
earnings, Twitch revenue,

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.800
YouTube revenue or any other source.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:48.060
Banks asserted that his company
had only made 60,000 dollars

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.230
on Tfue since the contract was signed.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.870
Tfue characterized the
contract as oppressive

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.560
since he's locked in for three years,

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.290
an initial six-month term

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.970
plus an additional 36 month extension

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.875
which FaZe Clan has already exercised

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:04.030
which means that he can't
compete for other teams.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.240
- This is about me in this contract.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.080
This contract that I signed
when I didn't know any better.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.980
I'm an idiot I should have
never signed in the first place.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.200
This three-year contract.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.740
- Tfue then initiated
two legal proceedings

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.870
against FaZe Clan.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.520
First he sued FaZe Clan in
court and filed a petition

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.490
with the California Labor Commission.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:27.040
The petition with the California
Labor Commission alleges

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.790
that Faze is acting as an
unlicensed talent agency

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.750
in violation of California labor laws

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.350
which are meant to protect entertainers

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.440
from gross exploitation.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.750
The petition asks the
California Labor Commission

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.180
to require the state to regulate FaZe Clan

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.900
like any other talent agency

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.440
and we'll come back to this later.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.340
The second action was a
standard lawsuit filed

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.120
in a Superior Court
for Los Angeles County.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:53.800
In it, Tfue raises seven
claims against FaZe Clan,

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.890
a claim or a cause of action in a lawsuit,

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.650
are, separate, independent reasons

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.880
for why a party asserts they are entitled

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.630
to win the lawsuit.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.720
It's normal to put more
than one of those claims

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.540
or causes of action in a lawsuit

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.610
even if the whole thing
sounds in breach of contract

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.340
as Tfue's claims basically do here.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.610
So first, Tfue is asking the court

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:17.630
for what's called a declaratory judgment

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.420
about the status of the gamer
agreement that he signed.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.670
A declaratory judgment
is when the court issues

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.640
an order determining the
relationship between the parties.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.520
A declaratory judgment is a
binding opinion about the rights

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.290
and responsibilities of two parties.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:32.950
Often you'll see this in
a breach of contract case

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.220
where the contract actually
hasn't been breached,

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.030
but it will be depending

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.560
on the different interpretations
of the two parties.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.250
In that kind of a case,
you go into court asking

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.690
for an actual declaration

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:48.360
even before the damages
haven't necessarily arisen.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.140
Tfue says that FaZe Clan
materially breached the agreement

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.320
by accepting money from third
parties for sponsorships

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.860
of Tfue involving modeling,
jewelry and apparel,

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.460
but according to Tfue after
he provided these services,

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.110
FaZe Clan did not distribute
any of the money to Tfue

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.627
in accordance with the agreement.

00:06:05.627 --> 00:06:08.360
Tfue's asking the court
for a declaratory judgment

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.760
that the contract was
breached by FaZe Clan

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:14.120
and is now void so he can get
out of any obligations he has

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.070
to fulfill the rest of his contract term.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:18.940
The second claim is a claim
for declaratory judgment

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:21.970
that the clauses in the
gamer agreement which pertain

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:26.580
to exclusivity and matching
rights violates section 16,600

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.060
of the California Business
and Professions Code.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.800
California is very
hostile to any agreement

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.550
that purports to limit a person's ability

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.250
to practice their profession.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:38.020
The contract has a
six-month non-compete clause

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.020
following termination and generally,

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.450
non-compete clauses are
illegal in California

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.520
except for when you have a non-compete

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.550
with an equity partner or like a CEO.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.740
As a result, it's very difficult

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.250
for any non-compete agreement

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.530
to pass muster under California law,

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.640
but there's also an issue in terms of

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.540
whether you can just void
the contract provision itself

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.680
or whether you have to avoid
the entire contract in general.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:04.010
Here, section 16,600
states that every contract

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.010
by which anyone is
restrained from engaging

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.211
in a lawful profession, trade
or business of any kind is

00:07:09.211 --> 00:07:11.370
to that extent void.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.920
Under the gamer agreement,
Tfue cannot contract

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.450
with another gaming company
without FaZe Clans consent.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.550
Tfue characterizes this and
other sections of the contract

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:21.380
as an illegal restraint on trade

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:24.960
and anti-competitive behavior
that violates section 16,600.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.320
The third claim is for a violation

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:31.490
of California Business and
Professions Code section 17,200

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.200
which precludes a person from engaging

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.600
in what's called unfair competition.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.660
All California lawyers know Business

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.900
and Professions Code section
7203 very, very well.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:44.560
It's basically a catch-all for
any shady business practices.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.170
It applies to any unlawful, unfair

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:49.740
or fraudulent business act or practice

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:53.674
and unfair, deceptive, untrue
or misleading advertising.

00:07:53.674 --> 00:07:57.360
Tfue alleges that FaZe Clan's
business practices embodied

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.920
by the gamer agreement have
restrained his business,

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.260
caused him financial losses and threatened

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:03.660
to cause other damages.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:07.050
Tfue wants the court to stop
FaZe Clans business practices

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:10.370
and pay him restitution
for any revenue and profits

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.880
that FaZe Clan made from
these business practices.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.780
One of the reasons you
would assert a claim

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.040
under Section 17,200 is that it gives you

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.710
what are called restitution damages

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:23.270
which are not necessarily
the same as contract damages.

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:26.050
Tfue's fourth cause of action is for money

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:28.440
that FaZe Clan collected
for sponsorship deals

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.690
that it did not give to Tfue.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.250
The fifth claim is for quantum merit.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.740
Quantum meruit is a latin term that means

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:37.740
as much as he deserved.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:40.450
It is an action to recover
the reasonable value

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:44.040
of services rendered by
one party to another.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.690
Tfue alleges that he provided
services to FaZe Clan

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.190
and other sponsors and that
those companies benefited

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.520
from those services,

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.870
but that Tfue did not receive compensation

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:54.880
for the value of those services.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.070
The sixth claim is for
breach of written contracts.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.160
In this claim, Tfue says that in the event

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.190
of the Court finds the
gamer agreement is valid

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:05.050
and enforceable, Tfue has done
everything that was required

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.460
to do under the agreement
while FaZe Clan has failed

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.210
to uphold its end of the bargain.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.290
Tfue is seeking money damages
for breach of contract.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:15.220
Finally, Tfue seventh cause of action is

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.375
for breach of fiduciary duty.

00:09:17.375 --> 00:09:19.260
Regardless of whether FaZe Clan

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.800
is considered a talent agency,

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.490
Tfue claims that it owed
him a fiduciary duty

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.840
to act in good faith and in
Tfue's interest at all times.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:29.970
By refusing a deal to avoid
making another sponsor upset,

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:32.090
the complaint alleges FaZe Clan acted

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:33.960
against Tfue's interest.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:37.120
So, do any of these claims hold water?

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.974
Well, all plaintiffs
write their complaints,

00:09:38.974 --> 00:09:41.300
that's the document that starts a lawsuit,

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.270
in a way that is favorable to their case

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.380
and almost certainly
leaves out any information

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.210
that's favorable to the defendant.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:50.750
So you have to look at these
lawsuits with a grain of salt.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.310
On the bridge of contract
allegations, if true,

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.640
they likely do give rise

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:57.360
to a material breach of the contract.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.290
Generally speaking,

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.740
when one party has materially
breached the contract,

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.570
it lets the other side off the
hook for further performance

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:06.330
and given Tfues newfound fame and success,

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.470
that's probably what he cares most about,

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:10.700
to get out of this onerous contract

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.330
so he can work with other people.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:15.570
The section 17,200 claim
is probably a catch-all

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.970
in case the breach of
contract claim fails.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:21.480
The quantum meruit claim
is to recover any funds

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.010
that wouldn't already be
covered by the contract

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.920
or if the court declares

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.570
that the contract is void ab initio,

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.840
in other words void from the beginning,

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:32.850
it's a cause of action
that would allow him

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:34.720
to recover what is fair

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:37.140
even if it's not actually
covered by the contract,

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.300
but the thrust of the allegations here are

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.880
for breach of contract.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:43.360
Asserting that FaZe Clan
has breached the contract

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.000
and therefore Tfue is free
to work with somebody else.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.650
A lot of people have
pointed out how quote,

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:51.670
unfair this contract is as a reason

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:54.040
for why the contract should be voided,

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.100
but Tfue isn't really arguing
that the contract is so unfair

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:59.030
as to be legally unenforceable.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:01.550
He's arguing, as he probably should,

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.380
that FaZe Clan breached the contract

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:04.960
and therefore it's void.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:07.180
There is actually a concept in the law

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.440
that voids a contract for unfairness,

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.990
it's called when a
contract is unconscionable.

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:14.350
In making this determination,

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.660
courts look at both the substantive
aspects of the contract.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.570
Are the terms on their
own unfair to one party,

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.770
as well as the procedural aspects

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.600
by which the contract was reached.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:27.770
Did the complaining party
have the time and or resources

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.630
to fully understand the contract.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.790
But you have to meet both the procedural

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.410
and substantive aspect
of unconscionability

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.505
in order for the court to
declare a contract as void.

00:11:37.505 --> 00:11:41.310
Tfue's contract doesn't
really fit that definition.

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:44.410
There is no real evidence
of procedural unfairness

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.920
like fraud or a contract of adhesion.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.759
Sure, the contract sucks for Tfue

00:11:48.759 --> 00:11:50.360
but it probably doesn't fit

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.440
the definition of unconscionable.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.720
For example, people
point to the 20, 80 split

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.540
of certain fees and winnings,

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:00.620
but that only matters
if Tfue actually won.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.190
Certain gamers might put
great value in the fact

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:06.570
that they get a guaranteed
2,000 dollars per month

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.680
and a court isn't likely
to second-guess that.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.500
That's why Tfue's
attorneys don't even bother

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.530
really making the argument

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.810
that this contract is unconscionable.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:19.590
Moreover, Tfue is a lot more
famous now than when he signed.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.350
So like a rookie contract
in regular sports,

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:23.380
FaZe Clan would argue

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.940
that the contract reflected
the party's positions

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.380
when the signer executed the contract

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.690
and certainly the uncertainty
of actually working

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:32.970
with Tfue at that stage in his career.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:36.320
And in addition to a guaranteed salary,

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:39.460
FaZe Clan would argue that
they gave him help and invested

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.180
in his future just like
you would in normal sports

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:45.490
when you take on a rookie
performer, but let's talk

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.430
about what potential
defenses FaZe Clan might have

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:50.490
to these assertions of breach of contract.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.100
What does FaZe Clan have
to say for its defense.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:53.933
Well first of all,

00:12:53.933 --> 00:12:55.960
FaZe Clan disputes Tfue's characterization

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.270
of the gamer agreement,
noting that it has been

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.450
in negotiation with Tfue's representatives

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.810
to offer him a new and better contract.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.280
FaZe Clan says that its previous
legal team was responsible

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:08.480
for the 80, 20 and 20, 80 split on profits

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:11.120
and after FaZe Clan got
new lawyers last summer,

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:12.740
its new contracts reversed the split

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:15.170
so that the game 80% of all of those deals

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.230
and FaZe Clan only gets 20%.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.660
FaZe Clan states that
just like any sports team

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.500
or movie company or record company,

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:24.270
its original deal with its
gamers is based on their talent

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.010
and their perceived value of that talent

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.600
at the time of the contract.

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:30.070
Like any entertainment
company or sports team,

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.900
FaZe Clan looks to renegotiate
a deal when the talent starts

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.300
to dramatically improve

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.550
and this is what the company
alleges it has done with Tfue.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:40.970
Now this isn't terribly
relevant to Tfue's allegations

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:44.030
that FaZe Clan actually
breached the contract

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:46.300
that they in fact executed.

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.240
It's in fact sort of an admission

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.230
that their current contract is unfair,

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:54.400
but since Tfue isn't really
arguing unconscionability,

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:57.340
it probably doesn't hurt them
too much to argue the optics

00:13:57.340 --> 00:14:00.070
of things and say that they're
offering a new contract.

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.780
In recognition of Tfue's
Fortnite abilities,

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.521
FaZe Clan says it has offered
him a seven-figure bonus

00:14:05.521 --> 00:14:08.210
and some options that give Tfue 100%

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:10.260
of any deals they negotiated for him.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.750
According to FaZe Clan,
Tfue has failed to respond

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.950
to any or all of these overtures.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.690
- [FaZe Clan] As early as
September 28th of last year,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:22.300
we sent the first revised
version of a contract for Tfue.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.070
We sent him a new agreement to his lawyer,

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.150
January 24th of this year.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:31.560
We sent another updated
thought on April third

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.697
then again on April 29th.

00:14:33.697 --> 00:14:36.473
We gave him so many different options

00:14:36.473 --> 00:14:40.980
that had little or even some
of them had no money going

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.190
to FaZe Clan and yet we still
couldn't get a deal done

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.930
and we come to find
that the reason why is,

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:50.060
he never planned on getting
a deal done with us.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:53.240
He wanted to start a
competing organization.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:56.410
- Now whether Tfue has
ignored FaZe Clans overtures

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.550
or whether he wants to
start a competing company

00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:02.020
as FaZe Clan alleges, probably
won't have much effect

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.520
on the lawsuit itself.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.500
The future conduct of the parties

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.560
doesn't really have much
bearing on the actual facts

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:11.010
as they exist now and in the past.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.620
FaZe Clan also disputes the notion

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.050
that the contracts are predatory.

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:15.990
In its Twitter statement,
the company notes

00:15:15.990 --> 00:15:17.630
that over the last several months,

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:19.840
it has encouraged any FaZe
Clan member interested

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.680
in hiring an outside
manager or agent to do so,

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:26.460
but FaZe Clan' best strategy
may be to actually lean in

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.850
to the draconian terms
of the current contract.

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:30.840
FaZe Clan recognizes the 50, 50 split

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:33.410
and sometimes 20, 80
split in the contract,

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:36.600
it argues that it has
never collected its 80%.

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:39.850
Now, assuming that FaZe
Clan actually upheld its end

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:43.240
of the bargain, FaZe
Clan could be entitled

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:46.530
to that 80% that's actually
written into the contract.

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.060
Now that the parties have broken up

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:49.577
and are going their separate ways,

00:15:49.577 --> 00:15:53.150
FaZe Clan could go after it's 80%

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.940
as written in the contract from Tfue.

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.130
After all, what does it have to lose.

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:01.280
Countersuing for 80% would give FaZe Clan

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.350
a bargaining chip against Tfue.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.120
Additionally, since FaZe
Clan and Tfue were unlikely

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:08.780
to ever get back together,
FaZe Clan will probably want

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.130
to counterclaim for any projected amounts

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.360
that Tfue would have made

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.940
during the remaining
period of the contract.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.800
- [FaZe Clan] Because we
were having these issues

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:20.350
and because we wanted Turner
to feel that we had his back,

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:23.574
we made the decision to
not collect any money

00:16:23.574 --> 00:16:27.460
under the under the old agreement,
nothing from prize pool,

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:29.756
nothing from YouTube,
nothing from anything

00:16:29.756 --> 00:16:32.800
except for a couple of
brand deals that accepted

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.297
that we only took 20% of

00:16:35.297 --> 00:16:38.380
and those deals came from us to him.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:42.860
- If FaZe Clan upheld its end
of the bargain in the contract

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.820
then it would be Tfue who is the one

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:48.270
who was breaching the agreement
by failing to play for FaZe

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.870
which would make him liable

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:51.780
for FaZe's expectation damages

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.990
during the remaining
years of the contract.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.420
Of course, that is a big if.

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:58.340
In either case, FaZe
Clan will want to show

00:16:58.340 --> 00:17:00.100
that it did not breach the contract

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:02.852
while Tfue will argue that
they did breach the contract.

00:17:02.852 --> 00:17:06.120
I can't opine on the
likelihood of either situation

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.290
because I don't know the underlying facts,

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.180
that's what the lawsuit is for.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.950
The crucial question in this litigation is

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.780
whether FaZe Clan upheld
its end of the bargain

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.426
and gave Tfue everything
he was entitled to

00:17:17.426 --> 00:17:19.340
under the contract.

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:21.017
The crucial question is not

00:17:21.017 --> 00:17:23.750
whether the contract is unfair to Tfue.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:26.270
Now, Tfue also filed a petition

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.700
with the California Labor Commissioner.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.600
Here, Tfue makes some bold allegations

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.920
about FaZe Clans activities.

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:35.270
Tfue says that he was pressured
to drink before he turned 21

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.300
and FaZe Clan encouraged
him and other residents

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:40.020
to gamble while on FaZe Clan property.

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:42.940
Tfue says that FaZe Clan
pressured and expected residents

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:45.430
of the FaZe house to
perform dangerous stunts

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:48.000
which resulted in Tfue's permanent injury.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.970
The Labor Commission petition argues

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:52.790
that gamers are entertainers and artists

00:17:52.790 --> 00:17:55.760
who must be represented by
licensed talent agencies

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.090
under California's Talent Agency Act

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.420
which regulates the relationship

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:01.710
between talent agencies and their clients.

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:04.320
For Tfue to be covered
by the Talent Agency Act

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.900
among other things, he
has to prove that he falls

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:09.820
under the definition of an
artist under that statute.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:11.990
To me, the Labor Commission petition seems

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.650
like the tail wagging the dog
in this litigation though.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.570
Certainly not an expert
in this particular niche

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.390
of California labor and employment law

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:21.210
so feel free to view my
analysis with skepticism here,

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:24.630
but I do know my way around
California litigation

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:27.120
and when you go to the
trouble of filing a lawsuit,

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:30.000
you tend to throw everything
that you have at it.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.490
Some arguments are better than
others and to me, it feels

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:35.463
like the Labor Commission
argument is colorable,

00:18:35.463 --> 00:18:37.140
but it's really just there

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.920
to back up the main
breach of contract claim.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.240
It's possible that this petition

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:42.570
could have wide-ranging effects

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:44.070
on the professional gamer community

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.960
if the Talent Agency Act
is expanding to cover them,

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.840
but this seems like a claim
that is probably going to settle

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.850
before getting to that
stage and setting a new law,

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:55.458
but we'll see how it unfolds.

